---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Resume | Steve Weiler"
  description="Download Steve Weiler's infrastructure engineering or software and systems engineering resume."
>
  <main>
    <section class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Professional Experience</p>
      <h1>Resume</h1>

      <p>
        More than 25 years of enterprise infrastructure experience combined
        with current software and systems engineering in Rust, Linux, AI,
        distributed systems, and application development.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-options" aria-label="Resume downloads">
      <article class="card resume-option">
        <div class="resume-option-header">
          <div class="project-badge">IE</div>

          <div>
            <p class="project-kicker">Systems &amp; Infrastructure</p>
            <h2>Infrastructure Engineering Resume</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          For Senior Systems Administrator, Systems Engineer, Linux
          Administrator, Infrastructure Engineer, Cloud Infrastructure,
          endpoint engineering, and platform operations roles.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>25+ years of enterprise systems administration</li>
          <li>Windows and Linux infrastructure</li>
          <li>VMware, storage, networking, and monitoring</li>
          <li>Microsoft 365 and cloud migrations</li>
          <li>Incident recovery and operational automation</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="actions">
          <a
            class="button"
            href="/resume/Steve-Weiler-Infrastructure-Resume.pdf"
            download
          >
            Download Infrastructure Resume
          </a>

          <a class="button secondary" href="/infrastructure/">
            View Infrastructure Experience
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card resume-option">
        <div class="resume-option-header">
          <div class="project-badge">SE</div>

          <div>
            <p class="project-kicker">Software &amp; Systems Engineering</p>
            <h2>Software Engineering Resume</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          For Rust Engineer, Systems Software Engineer, Linux Software
          Engineer, Platform Engineer, distributed systems, database,
          desktop platform, and AI infrastructure roles.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Rust and Linux systems programming</li>
          <li>Wayland compositor and desktop development</li>
          <li>Vector database and distributed-system design</li>
          <li>React, Node.js, C#, Go, and Python</li>
          <li>Local AI, IPC, graphics, and systems integration</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="actions">
          <a
            class="button"
            href="/resume/Steven-Weiler-Software-Resume.pdf"
            download
          >
            Download Software Resume
          </a>

          <a class="button secondary" href="/projects/">
            View Software Projects
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Combined Profile</p>
      <h2>Systems engineer and software developer</h2>

      <p>
        Systems engineer and software developer with more than 25 years of
        experience designing, implementing, modernizing, and supporting
        enterprise Windows and Linux infrastructure. Experienced in
        virtualization, networking, storage, monitoring, systems integration,
        enterprise applications, incident recovery, automation, and custom
        software development.
      </p>

      <p>
        Creator of FocalDesk, an open-source Wayland desktop environment
        written primarily in Rust, along with supporting projects involving
        vector search, local AI, desktop agents, web administration, IPC,
        graphics, and distributed-system architecture.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Technical Areas</p>
      <h2>Core expertise</h2>

      <div class="skill-groups">
        <div>
          <h3>Systems &amp; Infrastructure</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Linux and Windows Server</li>
            <li>Active Directory and Microsoft 365</li>
            <li>VMware ESXi and virtualization</li>
            <li>Networking, VLANs, VPNs, DNS, and DHCP</li>
            <li>Storage, monitoring, recovery, and migration</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Software Engineering</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Rust, C#, Go, Python, C, and C++</li>
            <li>Wayland, Smithay, OpenGL ES, and Linux graphics</li>
            <li>React, Node.js, IPC, and service architecture</li>
            <li>Databases, vector search, and distributed systems</li>
            <li>AI, machine learning, and local LLM integration</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Professional History</p>
      <h2>Experience</h2>

      <div class="experience-entry">
        <div class="experience-heading">
          <div>
            <h3>Account Coordinator</h3>
            <p class="project-kicker">Acrisure</p>
          </div>

          <p class="experience-date">2024–Present</p>
        </div>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Support Applied Epic and AMS360 workflows, policy servicing,
            carrier communication, documentation, and customer record
            maintenance.
          </li>
          <li>
            Transitioned into the position following organizational
            restructuring after the infrastructure environment moved to
            centralized corporate systems.
          </li>
          <li>Maintain an active Indiana Property and Casualty license.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-entry">
        <div class="experience-heading">
          <div>
            <h3>Service Desk Specialist</h3>
            <p class="project-kicker">Acrisure</p>
          </div>

          <p class="experience-date">2023–2024</p>
        </div>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Provided end-user support, incident resolution, access management,
            application troubleshooting, and ServiceNow documentation.
          </li>
          <li>
            Supported users during the transition from locally managed
            infrastructure to centralized cloud and corporate services.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-entry">
        <div class="experience-heading">
          <div>
            <h3>Systems Administrator</h3>
            <p class="project-kicker">
              United Insurance Agencies / Acrisure
            </p>
          </div>

          <p class="experience-date">1998–2023</p>
        </div>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Administered enterprise Windows and Linux systems, virtualization,
            networking, storage, monitoring, telephony, security, business
            applications, and user endpoints.
          </li>
          <li>
            Consolidated ten physical servers onto two VMware ESXi hosts and
            completed the production cutover in one day.
          </li>
          <li>
            Recovered data and restored operations following simultaneous
            storage-drive and dual-controller failures.
          </li>
          <li>
            Deployed OpenNMS with custom MIB monitoring for servers, storage,
            VoIP, VPNs, desktops, power, temperature, and humidity.
          </li>
          <li>
            Designed network segmentation for storage, voice, printers,
            guests, desktops, and other service groups.
          </li>
          <li>
            Built internal applications and integrations that reduced
            multi-hour operational processes to approximately 10–15 minutes.
          </li>
          <li>
            Supported migration of file services to SharePoint and OneDrive,
            email archiving to Exchange Online, and the decommissioning of the
            remaining data-center infrastructure.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>

        <h2>Master of Science in AI Engineering (Admitted)</h2>
        <p>
           Quantic School of Business and Technology<br>
           Awarded two scholarships; expected start 2026
        </p>

        <h2>Bachelor of Science</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Computer Science</strong><br>
          University of the People<br>
          April 2026
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Credentials</p>
        <h2>Certifications</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Certified Scrum Product Owner</li>
          <li>Certified ScrumMaster</li>
          <li>ICAgile Certified Professional</li>
          <li>Certificate of Cloud Security Knowledge</li>
          <li>Certificate of Competence in Zero Trust</li>
          <li>IBM AI Engineering Professional Certificate</li>
          <li>IBM Data Science Professional Certificate</li>
          <li>DeepLearning.AI TensorFlow Developer</li>
          <li>Indiana Property &amp; Casualty License</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .resume-options {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .resume-option {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .resume-option-header {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .resume-option-header h2 {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  }

  .resume-option ul {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .resume-option .actions {
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .skill-groups,
  .details-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .experience-entry + .experience-entry {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color, rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.25));
  }

  .experience-heading {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .experience-heading h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .experience-date {
    margin: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .resume-options,
    .skill-groups,
    .details-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .experience-heading {
      display: block;
    }

    .experience-date {
      margin-top: 0.4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
